From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/rockchip: vop2: Refuse mirroring a linear buffer on a Cluster window

A Cluster window takes its mirror bits from the AFBC decoder's rotate
mode register, which applies only to an AFBC buffer. A linear buffer
with REFLECT_X or REFLECT_Y passes the atomic check and is shown
unmirrored. Refuse the combination, so userspace mirrors it another way.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c
@@ -1309,6 +1309,13 @@
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
+	if (vop2_cluster_window(win) && !drm_is_afbc(fb->modifier) &&
+	    pstate->rotation & (DRM_MODE_REFLECT_X | DRM_MODE_REFLECT_Y)) {
+		drm_dbg_kms(vop2->drm,
+			    "Cluster windows mirror AFBC buffers only\n");
+		return -EINVAL;
+	}
+
 	if ((cstate->background_color << 16) &&
 	    (fb->format->has_alpha || pstate->alpha != 0xffff)) {
 		drm_dbg_kms(vop2->drm,
